# Generated files, none of which git is the source of.
#
# The rule: a file is committed when it is an INPUT — something a person wrote
# or accepted, that no command can recompute — and ignored when it is an
# OUTPUT, derived from the tree by a generator every reader runs first.
#
# An output in git is a file two branches rewrite in full on every change, so
# it conflicts on every merge and the conflict carries no information: the
# resolution is always "run the generator again". Over the last two hundred
# commits the two most-changed files in this repository were both outputs, and
# resolving them by hand is a step nobody can do correctly by reading it.
#
# What stays, because each is an input: `convention-baseline.json`, a count a
# person accepted with `--accept`; `blueprint-subjects.json`, which symbol each
# `@FollowsBlueprint` marker was accepted against, since a marker moved to a
# neighbouring function leaves every count identical; `seals.jsonl`, an
# attestation nothing can recompute because it records that a review happened;
# and the CloudFormation template snapshots, whose diff IS the review artefact.
#
# Where the outputs went instead: `pages.yml` regenerates and publishes every
# one of them on each push to `main`, so each still has an address, and the
# SessionStart hook regenerates them locally so agents and the blueprint hook
# read them from the tree. `--check` now means "validate without writing"
# rather than "compare against the committed copy", because there is no
# committed copy to compare against and a byte gate whose only subject is its
# own output proves nothing.
docs/architecture/*.html
docs/architecture/*-architecture.json
# The counts each diff run leaves for the index and the pull request comment to
# read. They describe a branch, like the diff page beside them, so there is no
# revision they would be true at.
docs/architecture/*-diff.json
.claude/skills/blueprint/blueprint-index.md
.claude/skills/blueprint/blueprint-coverage.html
.claude/skills/blueprint/blueprint-context.json
